<title>USA: Over 100,000 Maryland customers lose electricity.</title>
<headline>Over 100,000 Maryland customers lose electricity.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>More than 100,000 customers in central Maryland and Washington, D.C.'s northern suburbs were without electricity late Friday afternoon, utilities' spokespersons said.</p>
<p>Potomac Electric Power Co reported it had 50,000 customers without power in Montgomery County and in Washington, while a spokeswoman for Baltimore Gas and Electric Co said it had 49,000 customer without power late in the afternoon and had up to 93,000 outages earlier in the day.</p>
</text>
